      <h3>Account Terminated Due to Policy Violations</h3>
      <p>If your account is permanently terminated as a result of verified reports of policy violations the following refund policy applies:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>You will receive a prorated refund for the remaining complete months left in your subscription period</li>
        <li>The current partial month in which the termination occurs is not eligible for a refund</li>
        <li>Refunds are calculated based on the number of full calendar months remaining after the termination date</li>
        <li>Refunds are processed through Google Play and may take 5 to 10 business days to appear</li>
        <li>No refund is issued for token balances remaining in a terminated account</li>
        <li>No refund is issued if termination is due to extremely serious violations including but not limited to child exploitation, illegal content, or fraud</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="info-card purple">
        <p><strong>Refund example:</strong> If you have a yearly Personal Premium subscription and your account is terminated due to verified reports with 4 complete months remaining you will receive a refund equivalent to 4 months of the monthly equivalent price. The month in which termination occurred is not included in the refund calculation.</p>
      </div>

      <h3>Voluntary Cancellation</h3>
      <p>If you choose to cancel your subscription voluntarily your subscription will remain active until the end of the current billing period. No prorated refund is provided for voluntary cancellations. You must cancel through Google Play before your next renewal date to avoid being charged for the next period.</p>

      <h3>Refund Requests</h3>
      <p>All refund requests must be submitted within 30 days of the charge. Refund requests can be submitted to vorq2026@gmail.com with your account details and reason for the request. For Google Play purchases you may also request refunds directly through Google Play's refund process.</p>
